  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/mlca/glossary/catt%20pought">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type"/>
    <rdfs:label>catt pought (London Customs Accounts glossary)</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_catt_pought_cb3f30a1280d8293e004388b1d56a60895643814a3ee24f8f91a68f753b2dad6e1">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>The feet of a quadrupedal animal, characterized by being relatively compact feet with pads and claws, often configured so the weight of the animal is placed on the pad and toes rather than on a heel; examples are the feet of a bear, dog, or cat. [Source: Getty AAT]  fur made of the paws of the large wild mountain cat, the smaller wild cat or the domestic cat (Veale 218, 221)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
